data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"role": "model","parts": [{"text": "Thinking Process:\n\n1.  **Analyze the Request:**\n    *   **Goal:** Summarize the provided thoughts in the first person (\"I\").\n    *   **Length:** Maximum 50 words for the summary paragraph.\n    *   **Format:**\n        *   Header: 3-7 words, starts with a verb, wrapped in double asterisks (`**Header**`).\n        *   Two newlines (`\\n\\n`).\n        *   Plain text, single paragraph summary.\n    *   **Context:** Expert user, progress update, focus on recent updates, vary style/verbiage.\n    *   **Existing Summary:** None (empty).\n    *   **Constraints:** Never repeat a header (none used yet), never refer to instructions, only update on thoughts.\n    *   **Input Thoughts:** Analyzing a 3-box logic puzzle (boxes X, Y, Z; 1 gold, 2 stones; at most one label true; Clue A = X's label; Clue B = next clue to inspect; instructions start by reading Clue A).\n\n2.  **Drafting the Header:**\n    *   *Idea 1:* **Analyze the 3-box puzzle logic** (5 words) - Starts with verb \"Analyze\". Length: 5 words.\n    *   *Idea 2:* **Examine clues for box puzzle** (5 words) - Starts with verb \"Examine\". Length: 5 words.\n    *   *Let's use Idea 1:* `**Analyze the three-box logic puzzle**` (6 words).\n\n3.  **Drafting the Summary (First person, max 50 words, single paragraph):**\n    *   *Thoughts breakdown:* I'm setting up a logic puzzle with three boxes (X, Y, Z), one gold, two stones, and a constraint that at most one label is true. I've noted Clue A and Clue B's functions and am ready to trace the starting instructions.\n    *   *Drafting:* I am setting up the constraints for a three-box logic puzzle. With one gold, two stones, and at most one true label, I am mapping out how Clue A and Clue B dictate the inspection sequence. I will start by evaluating Clue A as instructed. (45 words)\n    *   *Check length:* 45 words. (Limit is 50).\n    *   *Check first person:* \"I am setting up...\", \"I am mapping...\", \"I will start...\" (Yes).\n    *   *Check style/verbiage:* Natural, expert-to-expert update.\n\n4.  **Refining and Formatting:**\n    *   Header: `**Analyze the three-box logic puzzle**`\n    *   Separator: `\\n\\n`\n    *   Body: `I am setting up the constraints for a three-box logic puzzle. With one gold, two stones, and at most one true label, I am mapping out how Clue A and Clue B dictate the inspection sequence. I will start by evaluating Clue A as instructed.`\n\n5.  **Final constraint check:**\n    *   First person? Yes.\n    *   Max 50 words? 45 words.\n    *   Header 3-7 words starting with a verb? \"Analyze the three-box logic puzzle\" -\u003e 6 words, starts with \"Analyze\".\n    *   Header wrapped in `**`? Yes.\n    *   Plain text single paragraph? Yes.\n    *   Separated by two newlines? Yes.\n    *   No instruction reference? Yes.**Analyze the three-box logic puzzle**\n\nI am setting up the constraints for a three-box logic puzzle. With one gold, two stones, and at most one true label, I am mapping out how Clue A and Clue B dictate the inspection sequence. I will start by evaluating Clue A as instructed.\n\n","thought": true}]}}],"usageMetadata": {"trafficType": "ON_DEMAND"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-carbon","createTime": "2026-11-11T10:39:53.643763Z","responseId": "-UX0arOlJ_yj9LsPrcel2AM"}

